{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775511011,"nonce":"gQCF5Tc6IO2Z6mSFojnB1ZXqp5I=","title":"Parse MCP signal tool calls in Codex adapter","message":"Parse MCP signal tool calls in Codex adapter\n\n## Context\nSignal protocol Phase 2: wire MCP signal detection into CodexAgent._parse_item(). Codex emits mcp_tool_call items with server=\"nightshift-signals\" and tool=\"nightshift_done\". Also register MCP server via codex mcp add in docker-entrypoint.sh.\n\nDepends on: 02c5e70 (MCP server shipped)\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_mcp_signal_done_emits_done_marker\n  Assert: an item.completed event with type \"mcp_tool_call\", server \"nightshift-signals\", tool \"nightshift_done\" produces AgentEvent with content \"@@DONE@@\"\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_mcp_signal_checkpoint_emits_checkpoint_marker\n  Assert: mcp_tool_call with tool \"nightshift_checkpoint\" and arguments {\"description\": \"progress\"} produces \"@@CHECKPOINT@@ progress\"\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_mcp_signal_question_emits_question_and_waiting\n  Assert: mcp_tool_call with tool \"nightshift_question\" produces \"@@QUESTION@@ ...\" then \"@@WAITING@@\"\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_non_signal_mcp_tool_parsed_as_system\n  Assert: mcp_tool_call with server \"other-server\" is parsed as SYSTEM (not a signal)\n- tests/test_entrypoint_codex_config.py::test_codex_mcp_registration\n  Assert: when AGENT_KIND=codex, docker-entrypoint.sh runs codex mcp add nightshift-signals\n\n## Files\n- adapters/agents/codex.py (modify — update _parse_item to handle mcp_tool_call)\n- docker-entrypoint.sh (modify — add codex mcp add in the AGENT_KIND=codex block)\n- core/constants.py (uses MCP_SIGNAL_SERVER_PREFIX from Phase 1b)\n\n## Implementation\n1. In CodexAgent._parse_item(), add a new block before the final return:\n   - Check item_type == \"mcp_tool_call\" and item.get(\"server\") == \"nightshift-signals\"\n   - Extract tool name from item.get(\"tool\", \"\")\n   - For nightshift_done: return AgentEvent(TEXT, \"@@DONE@@\")\n   - For nightshift_checkpoint: return AgentEvent(TEXT, f\"@@CHECKPOINT@@ {args.get('description', '')}\")\n   - For nightshift_question: store extra @@WAITING@@ event, return AgentEvent(TEXT, f\"@@QUESTION@@ {args.get('question', '')}\")\n   - Non-nightshift mcp_tool_call: return SYSTEM event\n2. In docker-entrypoint.sh, inside the `if [ \"$AGENT_KIND\" = \"codex\" ]` block, add after config.toml generation:\n   ```sh\n   codex mcp add nightshift-signals -- python3 /opt/nightshift/nightshift-mcp-server.py\n   ```\n\n## Patterns to follow\nSee existing _parse_item() in adapters/agents/codex.py:156-192.\nSee docs/signal-protocol-design.md \"Codex\" section for mcp_tool_call event format.\n\nREQ: REQ-004","files":null}]}